#: src/strings.md:1
msgid "Strings"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:3
msgid ""
"`'single'`, `\"double\"`, and `'''triple'''` quoted string literals are "
"supported. Unlike in recipe bodies, `{{…}}` interpolations are not supported "
"inside strings."
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:7
msgid "Double-quoted strings support escape sequences:"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:9
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"carriage-return   := \"\\r\"\n"
"double-quote      := \"\\\"\"\n"
"newline           := \"\\n\"\n"
"no-newline        := \"\\\n"
"\"\n"
"slash             := \"\\\\\"\n"
"tab               := \"\\t\"\n"
"unicode-codepoint := \"\\u{1F916}\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:20
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ just --evaluate\n"
"\"arriage-return   := \"\n"
"double-quote      := \"\"\"\n"
"newline           := \"\n"
"\"\n"
"no-newline        := \"\"\n"
"slash             := \"\\\"\n"
"tab               := \"     \"\n"
"unicode-codepoint := \"🤖\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:32
msgid ""
"The unicode character escape sequence `\\u{…}`<sup>1.36.0</sup> accepts up "
"to six hex digits."
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:35
msgid "Strings may contain line breaks:"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:37
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"single := '\n"
"hello\n"
"'\n"
"\n"
"double := \"\n"
"goodbye\n"
"\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:47
msgid "Single-quoted strings do not recognize escape sequences:"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:49
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"escapes := '\\t\\n\\r\\\"\\\\'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:53
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ just --evaluate\n"
"escapes := \"\\t\\n\\r\\\"\\\\\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:58
msgid ""
"Indented versions of both single- and double-quoted strings, delimited by "
"triple single- or double-quotes, are supported. Indented string lines are "
"stripped of a leading line break, and leading whitespace common to all non-"
"blank lines:"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:63
msgid ""
"```just\n"
"# this string will evaluate to `foo\\nbar\\n`\n"
"x := '''\n"
"  foo\n"
"  bar\n"
"'''\n"
"\n"
"# this string will evaluate to `abc\\n  wuv\\nxyz\\n`\n"
"y := \"\"\"\n"
"  abc\n"
"    wuv\n"
"  xyz\n"
"\"\"\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:78
msgid ""
"Similar to unindented strings, indented double-quoted strings process escape "
"sequences, and indented single-quoted strings ignore escape sequences. "
"Escape sequence processing takes place after unindentation. The "
"unindentation algorithm does not take escape-sequence produced whitespace or "
"newlines into account."
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:84
msgid "Shell-expanded strings"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:86
msgid "Strings prefixed with `x` are shell expanded<sup>1.27.0</sup>:"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:92
msgid "Value"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:92
msgid "Replacement"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:94
msgid "`$VAR`"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:94 src/strings.md:95
msgid "value of environment variable `VAR`"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:95
msgid "`${VAR}`"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:96
msgid "`${VAR:-DEFAULT}`"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:96
msgid "value of environment variable `VAR`, or `DEFAULT` if `VAR` is not set"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:97
msgid "Leading `~`"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:97
msgid "path to current user’s home directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:98
msgid "Leading `~USER`"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:98
msgid "path to `USER`’s home directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:100
msgid ""
"This expansion is performed at compile time, so variables from `.env` files "
"and exported `just` variables cannot be used. However, this allows shell "
"expanded strings to be used in places like settings and import paths, which "
"cannot depend on `just` variables and `.env` files."
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:105
msgid "Format strings"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:107
msgid "Strings prefixed with `f` are format strings<sup>1.44.0</sup>:"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:109
msgid ""
"```justfile\n"
"name := \"world\"\n"
"message := f'Hello, {{name}}!'\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:114
msgid ""
"Format strings may contain interpolations delimited with `{{…}}` that "
"contain expressions. Format strings evaluate to the concatenated string "
"fragments and evaluated expressions."
msgstr ""

#: src/strings.md:118
msgid "Use `{{{{` to include a literal `{{` in a format string:"
msgstr ""
